# Single-page app: serve index.html for the routes the client router knows (see SECTIONS in src/nav.js). "/" is index.html itself.
# There is deliberately NO catch-all "/* /index.html 200": with it every unknown URL answers 200, which search engines treat
# as a soft 404. Without it, an unknown path gets a real 404 status and public/404.html.
# Adding a page means adding its path here too, or reloading that page will 404 (npm run check:routes verifies this).

# Old, un-prefixed addresses (bookmarks from before the tools were split into sections): the app redirects them client-side
